# Slovak: Chron and Merit terminology

When writing or translating UI, email, Rules, glossary, or field strings into Slovak:

## Spelling

- **chron** (never *kron*, *krony*, *kronov*, …).
- **merit** (never *zásluha* / *zásluhy* for this product term).

## Casing

- Use lowercase mid-sentence: **chron** / **merit** and all declined forms.
- Capitalize only at the start of a sentence, glossary term headings, or short UI labels that are the whole string (e.g. msgstr `"Merity"`, `"Chrony"`).
- Do **not** treat them as proper nouns mid-sentence.
- English keeps **Chron(s)** / **Merit(s)**; Czech may keep title case unless aligned separately.

```text
❌ získate 10 kronov
✅ získate 10 chronov

❌ odmenu za Merit / prideľovať Merity
✅ odmenu za merit / prideľovať merity

❌ Vymeniť Chrony za národnú menu
✅ Vymeniť chrony za národnú menu
```

## Declension

**chron** — vzor *strom* (inanimate masculine); instrumental plural soft-style as used in product copy:

| Case | Singular | Plural |
|------|----------|--------|
| N | chron | chrony |
| G | chronu | chronov |
| D | chronu | chronom |
| A | chron | chrony |
| L | chrone | chronoch |
| I | chronom | chronmi |

**merit** — vzor *dub* (inanimate masculine):

| Case | Singular | Plural |
|------|----------|--------|
| N | merit | merity |
| G | meritu | meritov |
| D | meritu | meritom |
| A | merit | merity |
| L | merite | meritoch |
| I | meritom | meritmi |
